From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 07:50:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/17] panfrost: use 4-wide subgroups on Bifrost v7.0
 (Mali-G31, Mali-G51)

pan_subgroup_size() returns 8 for every v7 GPU, but only the v7.2 cores
(Mali-G76, Mali-G52) have 8-wide warps. Mali-G31 and Mali-G51 (v7.0) are
4-wide like v6. On a G31 the compiler then emitted the 8-lane subgroup
form of WMASK/CLPER, which faults the GPU with INSTR_INVALID_ENC (e.g.
dEQP-VK.subgroups.basic.compute.subgroupelect), and lowered
subgroup id/size/num_subgroups, nir_lower_subgroups and the divergent
indirect lowering with the wrong width. The 4-lane period is also visible
in OpenCL: lanes are lost in groups of four when a warp diverges.

Add pan_subgroup_size_gpu(gpu_id) and use it wherever the GPU is known:
the Bifrost compiler, gallium (rusticl subgroup sizes, shader info) and
panvk (subgroupSize, min/maxSubgroupSize, shaderWarpsPerCore and
executable properties).

Generated-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
